      "note": "Separated from the RANS record because a wall function is configured independently of both LES and RANS, and because the RANS runtime update is incomplete while this treatment is separately usable. The velocity laws and their friction-velocity root-finds carry unit coverage, and the integration that applies them across the six faces is covered by tests/c/test_boundaries.c, which checks that the corrected first-interior velocity is the modelled profile at that cell's wall distance. Status is experimental rather than supported because no reference-flow comparison has been run, no shipped case enables it, and only the log law is reachable: the Cabot and Werner-Wengle kernels exist and are unit-tested but the integration dispatches to the log law unconditionally. The pass now records the friction velocity as the catalogued field `Utau` and writes near-wall statistics to <run.runtime_logs>/wall_model.csv, including the first-cell y+ that says whether the selected law is being applied where it is valid; before that, u_tau was computed every step and discarded, so no wall diagnostic existed. Its storage was also allocated from the dof-3 DM while every reader opened it through the dof-1 DM, a pairing PETSc rejects, so enabling wall functions on a case with a WALL face aborted; tests/c/test_boundaries.c now allocates the way production does and compares the allocation against the field catalog descriptor, which is what makes that class of mismatch fail in the suite. A toy channel exercising all three laws end to end found two defects that unit coverage could not reach. Werner-Wengle reported one identical u_tau at every wall cell, because wall_function() used its Newton initial guess as the answer; it now uses the closed-form taw_Werner()/u_Werner_explicit() pair, which is the Werner-Wengle model proper - the profile integrated across the first cell inverts without any root-find, realising the no-inner-iteration property the model is chosen for. The earlier iterative helpers are retained, unwired, with the reasons recorded at their definitions: their branch threshold depends on the friction velocity being solved for, and their two branches invert different relations, so they reconstruct the pointwise profile only below y+ = 11.81. Separately, the friction-velocity storage was allocated inside the LES/RANS block, so enabling a wall model without either of them left ApplyWallFunction dereferencing a null vector; allocation is now gated on the wall model alone, which is what the schema has always said. All three laws now produce friction velocities that vary cell to cell and differ from one another at y+ ~ 10-14, and agree exactly at y+ ~ 1.4 where every wall model must reduce to u+ = y+. None of this is validation against a reference flow, which has still not been run."
    },
