        },
        "scientific_verification": {
          "not_applicable": "Nothing logging produces is a scientific claim of its own; it reports quantities the subsystems that compute them are separately accountable for. Its own contracts - level gating, allow-list behaviour, snapshot cadence, string conversion - are behavioural and are covered by tests/c/test_logging.c rather than by physical validation."
        }
      },
      "note": "Registered as its own subsystem because every other module reports through it while nothing depends on it for a result, which is exactly the shape that leaves a module unowned: before this record it appeared in no subsystem, no capability family, no contract, no freshness surface, and in neither src/guide.md nor the module map of 13_Code_Architecture, despite owning the console tier system, the runtime metric emitters, and the lifecycle of every file in <run.runtime_logs>. A change to what a user sees therefore tripped no staleness suspicion anywhere. Status is supported rather than experimental because the console contracts carry direct unit coverage in tests/c/test_logging.c and the configuration surface has been stable and user-facing across releases; the claim is about those behavioural contracts, not about the correctness of any quantity another subsystem hands it to print."
    }
